INT. MOUNTAIN SKI-LIFT CHALET - NIGHT

A pine-paneled lodge, snow banked against the windows. Fire in a stone hearth. A cracked leather sofa, a bar of antlers, a pot of mulled wine on the stove.

Five people. One is a stranger.

ADELINA RUSSO-OKAFOR (30s, red scarf, cheeks wind-burned) kneels at the hearth, feeding the fire. HOLDEN MBEKI-FALK (30s, ski patrol jacket, radio at his shoulder) paces by the window. ROSEMARY PLUMMER-ASANTE (60s, lodge owner, tartan apron) ladles wine into mugs. TEODORO BRANDT-NWOSU (20s, snowboarder, one arm in a sling) sprawls on the sofa. And near the door, dripping, stands a MAN IN A GREY COAT (40s, no hat, snow in his eyebrows) who arrived ten minutes ago and has not given a name.

ROSEMARY
Wine, love?

MAN IN A GREY COAT
Thank you.

He takes it. Does not drink. Adelina watches him over her shoulder.

ADELINA
Where did you come from?

MAN IN A GREY COAT
Down the mountain.

ADELINA
The lift's been closed for hours.

MAN IN A GREY COAT
I walked.

HOLDEN
In this?

MAN IN A GREY COAT
It wasn't so bad.

Teodoro whistles. Rosemary exchanges a look with Holden.

ROSEMARY
You'll be wanting a room.

MAN IN A GREY COAT
No. I'm only waiting.

HOLDEN
For what?

MAN IN A GREY COAT
For her.

He nods at Adelina. She goes very still. The fire pops.

ADELINA
I don't know you.

MAN IN A GREY COAT
No.

ADELINA
Then why--

MAN IN A GREY COAT
I knew your sister.

Silence. Rosemary lowers the ladle. Teodoro sits up. Holden's hand finds his radio.

ADELINA
My sister died in the spring.

MAN IN A GREY COAT
I know. I was there.

Adelina stands, slowly. Her scarf slides from her shoulders. Holden steps between them, not hostile, but ready.

HOLDEN
Sir, maybe you should sit down.

MAN IN A GREY COAT
Of course.

He sits on the arm of the sofa. Teodoro shifts to make room, then thinks better of it and shifts back.

ADELINA
Say your name.

MAN IN A GREY COAT
Callum.

ADELINA
(testing it)
Callum.

CALLUM
She talked about you. Every day.

ADELINA
That's not possible.

CALLUM
She called you her lighthouse.

Adelina closes her eyes. The room holds its breath. Rosemary crosses herself. Holden's hand drops from the radio.

CALLUM (CONT'D)
She wanted you to have this.

He reaches into his coat and takes out a small, flat parcel wrapped in brown paper, tied with string. He holds it out. For a long moment, she doesn't take it.

Then she does.
